# Rule: SwiftUI State Management & Data Flow

Sources

https://developer.apple.com/tutorials/swiftui-concepts/driving-changes-in-your-ui-with-state-and-bindings
https://developer.apple.com/tutorials/swiftui-concepts/creating-a-custom-input-control-that-binds-to-a-value
https://developer.apple.com/tutorials/swiftui-concepts/defining-the-source-of-truth-using-a-custom-binding
https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/model-data

Core Principle

Every mutable UI value must have a clear source of truth.

Rules

- Own state at the highest level that truly needs to own it, and no higher.
- Prefer local state for local UI behavior.
- Pass immutable values to children that only display data.
- Pass bindings only to children that need write access.
- Use custom bindings to adapt or project owned state without duplicating it.
- Keep model-backed state separate from ephemeral UI-only state.
- Do not create multiple competing sources of truth for the same concept.

Anti-Patterns

- Duplicated mutable state in parent and child.
- Binding-everything by default.
- Local shadow copies of model data that must stay manually synced.
- Reusable inputs that own edited value internally instead of binding outward.
